<p class="lt-chem-13446">Now that we have a listing of all of the microstates, we need to figure out how to divide them up between the term symbols. It turns out that each term symbol can have, at most, one microstate from each box on the chart. The term symbols always end up claiming a &ldquo;box&rdquo; of microstates, centered on the middle of the chart. This is easier shown than said.</p>

<p class="lt-chem-13446">Attacking the chart from the top, we can see that the \(M_l = 4\) \(M_s = 0\) state clearly belongs to a \(^1G\) symbol. The \(M_l = &#8208;4\) \(M_s =0\) box also clearly belongs to this symbol. If I connect these states with a &ldquo;box,&rdquo; I get this:</p>

